{"id":1004,"date":"2016-06-28T20:36:26","date_gmt":"2016-06-28T20:36:26","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?p=1004"},"modified":"2021-06-10T12:42:40","modified_gmt":"2021-06-10T12:42:40","slug":"aims-ghana-organises-mathematics-teacher-training-workshop-in-wa","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/aims-ghana-organises-mathematics-teacher-training-workshop-in-wa\/","title":{"rendered":"AIMS Ghana Organises Mathematics Teacher Training Workshop in Wa"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>The African Institute for Mathematical Sciences Ghana, in partnership with the Government of Ghana organised the second mathematics workshop for basic school teachers in the Upper West Regional capital, Wa. A total of fifty teachers from Wa West district participated in the intensive workshop from 23rd to 27th November 2015.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/15\/2017\/06\/wa-grp-0.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-902\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>Renowned trainers from AIMS guided the teachers in using simple approaches to teaching topics including fractions, word problem, factorisation, and computer based mathematics through creative and engaging teaching methods.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The workshop in Wa follows a very successful pilot workshop in Donkokrom, in the Eastern Region.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The African Institute for Mathematical Sciences Ghana, in partnership with the Government of Ghana organised the second mathematics workshop for basic school teachers in the Upper West Regional capital, Wa. A total of fifty teachers from Wa West district participated in the intensive workshop from 23rd to 27th November 2015. Renowned trainers from AIMS guided<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":1005,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta